WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.800
We begin with

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.935
the president of the United States.

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:02.836
Just moments ago,

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:03.336
the president

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.472
leaving on a critical overseas trip,

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:06.573
but a trip

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.507
he is cutting short

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.075
because of the looming crisis

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.710
about the debt here at home.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.011
Today,

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.612
the president says he cut that trip short

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.581
to be back for the final negotiations

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.682
on the debt ceiling.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:16.983
Right now, new key

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.318
negotiators are meeting up

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:19.486
on Capitol Hill.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:20.220
The last hour,

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.955
the president said he is now confident

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:23.390
there will be an agreement

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.457
and that the United States

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.493
will not default.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.796
America is not a deadbeat nation.

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.564
We pay our bills.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.500
Nation is never default on its debt

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.001
and never will.

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:35.869
And we're going to continue

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:36.669
these discussions

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.771
with congressional leaders

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:38.872
in the coming days.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:40.106
Until we reach an agreement.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:41.875
The House

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:42.842
speaker, Kevin McCarthy,

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.277
decided not to let the president

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.945
have the last word as the president.

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.147
Just after the president finished

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:49.549
speaking, McCarthy says it's about time.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:52.619
The president's negotiating team

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:54.087
now, the president

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:54.888
and leader Schumer,

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:55.955
have finally backed off

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.824
the idea that they won't negotiate.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:00.093
They finally backed off the insane,

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:03.730
un rational and sensible idea

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.067
that you just raise the debt ceiling.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:07.801
Let's begin our coverage

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:08.935
with CNN's Jeremy Diamond.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.770
He's live at the White House for us.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.405
So a victory for the process,

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:12.872
if you will,

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.741
Jeremy, progress on the process.

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:17.310
The question is, what about the substance

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.478
that is the big question, John.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:19.312
And to be sure,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.314
there are still so many talking points

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:22.615
with just 15 days

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.517
potentially until the United States

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.518
defaults on its debt.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.821
If indeed that June 1st deadline stands.

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:28.822
But today, the president

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.190
expressing confidence

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.058
that the United States will not default,

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.660
mainly because he says there's

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.427
no alternative.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.129
The United States can't default

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.230
on its debt

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.833
And he also noted that yesterday

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.634
we heard several leaders come out and say

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.702
that all of the leaders,

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.604
including the speaker of the House,

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:45.438
acknowledge

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.540
that the consequences of default

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:49.375
would indeed be catastrophic.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.410
In line with that, President

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.578
Biden has now elevated

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:53.046
these negotiations

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:55.248
to three senior staff members.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:55.915
The president's

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.417
counselor, Steve Ricchetti,

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:59.586
his director of the Office of Management

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.421
and Budget, Shalanda Young,

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:02.489
as well as

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.023
the director of legislative affairs,

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:05.024
Louisa Terrell.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:07.260
On the other side for Speaker McCarthy,

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.328
you have Congressman

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:10.530
Garret Graves, as well as the speaker's

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.731
senior staff.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.632
But the president

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.200
nonetheless, in an acknowledgment

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:14.901
that this deal

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.202
is going to come down

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.904
to him and Kevin McCarthy

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.873
cutting that trip short,

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:22.375
going only to Japan, not going forward

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.176
with those stops

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.278
to Papua New Guinea and Australia.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:25.645
And that's

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:26.613
because he wants to be back

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.214
for the final negotiations,

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.049
which are expected to happen

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:32.552
next week if indeed a deal is to be had.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:33.920
At the same time, John,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:34.754
as you just heard

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:36.156
from the speaker of the House,

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:36.890
he is saying, look,

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.191
the White House is finally willing

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:38.892
to negotiate.

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.260
They've dropped this pretense

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:40.827
that they are not

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:42.228
negotiating over the debt,

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.163
not quite here.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:43.997
If you talk to folks here

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:44.464
at the White House,

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:45.331
they still insist

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.367
they are not negotiating over default.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:48.868
Nonetheless, what's clear

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:49.969
is that they are negotiating

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.204
over the spending agreement

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:51.571
with that

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:52.438
ticking time

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.607
bomb of the potential for default,

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:56.543
hanging over them. John.

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:57.143
Jeremy Diamond,

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.044
kick us off to the White House.

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:58.745
Jeremy, thank you.

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.213
Let's bring the conversation in the room

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.447
with me to share their reporting

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:02.549
and their insights, CNN's

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:03.416
Melody Senator

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.485
Francesca Chambers of USA Today and

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:06.819
Margaret Talev of Axios.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:08.621
The idea that you're

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.190
negotiating the budget or the debt,

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.624
let's just say that's a difference

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:12.792
without a distinction or a distinction

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:13.393
without a difference.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:14.394
Call it what you will.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:15.261
My question is Kevin

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:16.296
McCarthy gets a big win

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:17.764
here on the process,

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:18.831
direct negotiations

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.333
between the White House team

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:20.800
and people

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.168
he trusts on the White House team

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:23.203
and the speaker's office.

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:24.504
The question is how much wiggle room

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:25.772
does Kevin McCarthy have

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.839
on the substance?

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.107
Because the House Republicans

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:28.708
are not going to get

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:29.542
everything they want.

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:30.443
They're not going to get everything

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:30.777
they want.

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:31.411
Whatever they do

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:31.978
come up with,

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.246
there's going to be a sales job

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.047
that Kevin McCarthy

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:35.148
has to do to his conference.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:36.115
They've been trying to lower

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.317
the expectation, particularly

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:38.618
among conservatives, that

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:39.652
what they pass in

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:39.986
the House

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.487
is not going to be the final deal,

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:42.088
that they're going to

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:43.022
have to be flexible.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:45.058
This is going to take some compromise.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:45.558
You're right

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:46.960
that there is a small step

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.194
forward in terms of process

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:48.695
and structure.

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:50.129
This is what Kevin McCarthy wanted

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:50.563
all along.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:52.498
He wanted it to just be him

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.067
and President Biden negotiated

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.236
because he sees Biden as more flexible

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.036
than some of these other

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:57.837
Democratic leaders.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:58.938
And case in point,

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.373
Biden is still leaving the door

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:01.674
open to potentially

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.676
some form of work requirements.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:04.310
Which is something

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.378
that Democratic leaders

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:06.579
are warning against, saying

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:07.880
it's a nonstarter for them.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.515
But Kevin McCarthy feels like

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:10.717
he has an upper hand right now

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:12.752
and that he can get Biden to a good place

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:13.486
to that point.

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:14.854
The president over the weekend said, hey,

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:16.589
I voted for work requirements and welfare

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.024
reform back in the eighties.

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:19.292
The White House said, oh, gosh.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.627
And they scramble to try to quiet

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:21.661
progressive complaints.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:22.428
They issued a statement

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:23.196
yesterday afternoon

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:23.763
saying the president

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:24.731
was not going to accept work

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:25.231
requirements.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.966
Speaker McCarthy says it's a red line.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.101
Today, as Melanie notes,

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:29.335
the president opened the door

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:30.803
maybe just a little bit. He opened it

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.673
I'm not going to accept

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:34.741
any work requirements

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:37.910
that's going to impact on mental health

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:39.045
needs of people.

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:40.113
I voted years ago

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:42.348
for the work requirements that exist

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:43.383
but it's possible

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:44.484
there could be a few others,

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:47.520
but not anything of any consequence.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.755
Do we have any definition

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:49.555
of what he means?

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.190
There is, he said, medical.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.592
So I assume he means Medicaid.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.092
That's right.

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:54.027
We'll see if that plays out.

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.495
But snap or food

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:56.729
stamps or food assistance,

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:57.463
that's another area

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:58.531
Republicans are looking for.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.565
Is that with the president's

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:00.033
opening there

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:01.034
or are we waiting for the White House

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:02.001
to clean it up again?

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:02.702
He's not.

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.637
So a White House official tells me

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:06.639
that the president thinks

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:07.974
that there could be some possibility

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:09.409
in other potential areas.

00:05:09.409 --> 00:05:11.444
But as he went on to say nothing, of

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:12.378
of consequence.

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:13.079
So snap.

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:15.848
No Tanev, no Medicaid.

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:18.251
No, he's not willing to go beyond

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:19.886
what he already voted for there.

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:21.154
Now, one area

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:22.822
that the White House is signaling

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:23.990
that they could negotiate

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:24.991
with Republicans on

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:26.526
is those spending caps

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:28.661
they might be willing to agree

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:29.529
to a spending cap.

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:31.331
Now, the question of that would be for

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.632
how long is this one year?

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:33.633
Is this ten years?

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:34.634
But that is where you could see

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:35.768
some potential movement.

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:36.536
The White House wants it

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:37.470
to be one or two years

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.771
that you get through the next election.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:39.739
They hope they win.

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:40.907
They hope the Democrats pick up.

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:41.841
This is part of the dance

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:43.443
everyone's thinking about 20, 24.

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:44.977
But we can go back to just the new

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:45.912
the president's new team,

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:46.412
his budget

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:47.313
director, Shalanda

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:48.081
Young, who has deep

00:05:48.081 --> 00:05:49.148
experience up on Capitol

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:50.216
Hill, a deep respect

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:51.551
among a lot of the Republicans out there.

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:52.151
Steve Ricchetti,

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:53.319
I know Steve from the Bill Clinton

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:53.953
White House

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.154
and he's been around a long time

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:55.888
and Republicans

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:57.190
have been in a lot of negotiations

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:57.990
with him.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.258
Louisa Terrell is the president's

00:05:59.258 --> 00:06:00.226
legislative affairs director.

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:00.827
Garret Graves

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:01.728
is one of the speaker's

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:03.062
most trusted fellow House

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:04.364
Republicans there.

00:06:04.364 --> 00:06:05.498
Let me put it this way.

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:06.966
You have adults in the room

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:08.301
who know how to negotiate.

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:09.802
The question is, why did it take so long?

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.137
Because everyone was in this dance over

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:12.238
whether or not were going to negotiate.

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:13.506
Yeah, because who's going to blink first?

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:14.741
But look, I mean, you have to

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:16.309
there is something

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:17.343
that will get everyone

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:18.644
across the finish line.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:19.579
For Kevin McCarthy,

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:21.013
it's to maintain the speakership.

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:22.615
He needs to bring enough of his caucus

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:24.417
along that he doesn't lose power.

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:25.885
For Joe Biden, it's two things

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:27.453
not to have a default

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.222
and to get this postponed to

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.690
this never has to happen again

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:31.758
until after

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:33.493
the next presidential election.

00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:35.194
Those two things are a win for Joe Biden.

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:36.796
Why does he keep opening the door?

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:38.131
Is it just because he's gaffe prone

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:39.132
or can't help himself?

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:39.766
I don't think so.

00:06:39.766 --> 00:06:41.100
It's because we have now

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.535
30 some years of polling,

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:44.036
but at least five or six

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:46.506
consistent years of immediate polling

00:06:46.706 --> 00:06:47.106
that show

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:48.241
that actually Americans

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:48.708
don't think

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:50.209
that people should have a free ride,

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:51.511
that the way you packages

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:52.912
and talk about this matters

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:55.081
and that if for better or for worse, it's

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:55.848
usually for worse.

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:57.316
There are two Americas.

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:59.585
McCarthy is messaging to different voters

00:06:59.819 --> 00:07:01.187
than Joe Biden is.

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:02.622
And what President Biden,

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:04.857
I think, is trying to make clear is

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:06.459
he is willing to

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:09.095
talk about

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:10.096
language to suggest

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:12.231
that everybody try to work if they can.

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:13.299
But he is not going to leave

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:14.267
anyone destitute

